  [iter1] $5.17, 50 turns, 2007s; run total $8.36
I widened the operand DMA bursts in `dma_ld` to unroll over 4 rows (64 bytes) per iteration, perfectly maxing out the 512-bit wide AXI bus that Vitis infers from `align_value(64)`. I used a ceiling division `(na + 3) >> 2` for the trip counts, ensuring it still correctly loads the required data for vector and random programs whose operand bounds are not multiples of 4 (safely fetching padding within the `MAXDIM` matrix bound). This cuts the serial operand staging bottleneck by ~75%, lowering the RTL cosim cycles at 16x16x16 from 686 to 627, and does not depend on tests failing to exercise corners.
